1
00:00:00,197 --> 00:00:01,217
(Sheldon:)That's Leonard's.

2
00:00:02,132 --> 00:00:04,062
(Amy:)Children's toy.

3
00:00:04,601 --> 00:00:09,591
(Sheldon:)One Game of Thrones
collector's edition Longclaw sword.

4
00:00:09,840 --> 00:00:12,370
(Sheldon:)Leonard and I bought that together.

5
00:00:12,576 --> 00:00:15,066
(Sheldon:)That's a bit of an ethical conundrum.

6
00:00:16,280 --> 00:00:17,910
(Sheldon:)I'll keep it.

7
00:00:18,649 --> 00:00:20,709
So, what's your plan moving forward?

8
00:00:20,918 --> 00:00:24,248
I suppose I'll have to find and cultivate
a new roommate.

9
00:00:24,454 --> 00:00:26,214
(Sheldon:)What a task that will be.

10
00:00:26,423 --> 00:00:29,913
(Sheldon:)Do you know how uncivilized
Leonard was when I took him in?

11
00:00:30,861 --> 00:00:32,851
(Sheldon:)- No.
- It took me forever...

12
00:00:33,063 --> 00:00:35,093
(Sheldon:)...to get him on a bathroom schedule.

13
00:00:35,799 --> 00:00:38,999
(Sheldon:)He would just go
whenever the mood struck him.

14
00:00:40,003 --> 00:00:43,233
- Like a dog boy.
- Exactly.

15
00:00:43,440 --> 00:00:46,600
(Amy:)What if you could find a roommate
who was a scientist...

16
00:00:46,810 --> 00:00:49,400
(Amy:)...and already familiar and comfortable
with your ways?

17
00:00:49,613 --> 00:00:50,983
(Sheldon:)That would be ideal.

18
00:00:51,181 --> 00:00:56,411
(Sheldon:)If a person like that existed,
I would sign on, no further questions asked.

19
00:00:56,620 --> 00:01:04,020
(Amy:)Great, here I am.

